{"uid":"8e950ac2ccc48eca","name":"test_run_detail_hides_the_terminal_record_during_the_finishing_window","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_run_detail_hides_the_terminal_record_during_the_finishing_window","historyId":"ab884d402436856a62efb324f2643e2b","time":{"start":1791941647641,"stop":1791941657233,"duration":9592},"description":"Task 015 (#56): task 012's `finishing` state settles `verdict`/`endedAt`\n    into status.json before the post-terminal reflect iteration is actually\n    over -- so a run whose `currentIteration` is still a live dict (the\n    reflect iteration itself, still running) must not have the run-detail\n    card show a colored, terminal-looking verdict pill or an `ended:` row: an\n    operator reading the card must not conclude the run is over while the\n    timeline right below it is still showing that very iteration as\n    'running...'. Neither field is hidden -- the verdict TEXT is still shown,\n    just not styled as the same pill a genuinely terminal run gets -- and both\n    reappear once the window closes (state promotes, currentIteration clears).","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 015 (#56): task 012's <code>finishing</code> state settles <code>verdict</code>/<code>endedAt</code><br />\ninto status.json before the post-terminal reflect iteration is actually<br />\nover -- so a run whose <code>currentIteration</code> is still a live dict (the<br />\nreflect iteration itself, still running) must not have the run-detail<br />\ncard show a colored, terminal-looking verdict pill or an <code>ended:</code> row: an<br />\noperator reading the card must not conclude the run is over while the<br />\ntimeline right below it is still showing that very iteration as<br />\n'running...'. Neither field is hidden -- the verdict TEXT is still shown,<br />\njust not styled as the same pill a genuinely terminal run gets -- and both<br />\nreappear once the window closes (state promotes, currentIteration clears).</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"new